{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ROM",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Know ye not, brethren, (for I speak to them that know the law) that the law hath dominion over a man as long as he liveth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the woman who hath a husband, is bound by the law to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "her",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " husband so long as he liveth; but if the husband is dead, she is loosed from the law of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "her",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " husband.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So then, if while ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "her",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " husband liveth, she is married to another man, she shall be called an adulteress: but if her husband is dead, she is free from that law; so that she is no adulteress, though she be married to another man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore, my brethren, ye also are become dead to the law by the body of Christ; that ye should be married to another, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to him who is raised from the dead, that we should bring forth fruit to God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For when we were in the flesh, the motions of sins, which were by the law, did work in our members to bring forth fruit to death:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now we are delivered from the law, that being dead by which we were held; that we should serve in newness of spirit, and not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the oldness of the letter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What shall we say then? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the law sin? By no means. No, I had not known sin, but by the law: for I had not known lust, except the law had said, Thou shalt not covet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But sin, taking occasion by the commandment, wrought in me all manner of concupiscence. For without the law sin ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " dead.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I was alive without the law once: but when the commandment came, sin revived, and I died.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the commandment which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was ordained",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to life, I found ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For sin, taking occasion by the commandment, deceived me, and by it slew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore the law ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " holy, and the commandment holy, and just, and good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Was then that which is good made death to me? By no means. But sin, that it might appear sin, working death in me by that which is good; that sin by the commandment might become exceeding sinful.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we know that the law is spiritual: but I am carnal, sold under sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For that which I do, I allow not: for what I would, that I do not; but what I hate, that I do.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If then I do that which I would not, I consent to the law that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now then it is no more I that do it, but sin that dwelleth in me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I know that in me (that is, in my flesh,) dwelleth no good thing: for to will is present with me; but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "how",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to perform that which is good, I find not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the good that I would, I do not; but the evil which I would not, that I do.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now if I do that which I would not, it is no more I that do it, but sin that dwelleth in me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I find then a law, that when I would do good, evil is present with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I delight in the law of God, after the inward man:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I see another law in my members warring against the law of my mind, and bringing me into captivity to the law of sin which is in my members.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O wretched man that I am! who shall deliver me from the body of this death?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.7.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.7.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I thank God, through Jesus Christ our Lord. So then, with the mind I myself serve the law of God; but with the flesh the law of sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
